      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>True standardized RGO square-root density domains</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For the true source RGO posterior standardized using the same internally produced measurable stationary proximal point, produce the actual relative Gaussian density, positive partition, C2 square root and all L2/entropy/gradient domains with the exact1/4 energy, for every eta(s)&gt;0.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[r_s=(x\mapsto\eta_s^{-1/2}(x-p_s))_\#R_s=q_s\gamma,\quad q_s=e^{-\rho_s}/Z_s,\quad\nabla\log q_s=-\nabla\rho_s,\quad\int\|\nabla\sqrt{q_s}\|^2d\gamma=\tfrac14\int\|\nabla\rho_s\|^2dr_s.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Reuse the true posterior and the same stationary point</strong><p>The existing allpositive true standardized RGO producer constructs a measurable p with p+eta gradVp=y. Its literal affine pushforward r is the actual volume Gibbs law of norm²/2+rho, and its residual is C2 with gradientrho0=0 and Hessian0..eta. The residual value at0 is computed from its definition.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Apply the new density-domain producer to that actual residual</strong><p>Instantiate the shared theorem with L=eta(s) and the same actual rho. Its canonical volume-law equality agrees with the true affine posterior law, yielding r=gamma.tilted(-rho), the actual normalized q, all square-root/entropy domains and actual probability. No output density or moment certificate is supplied.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Keep the same law in every derivative and energy conclusion</strong><p>Transport only measure-valued fields along the proved actual-law equality. f_s and both gradients retain their literal representatives, and the exact1/4 energy uses that same true r_s. The measurable family is an authored extension; fixed parameters follow by Unit specialization. No eta upper cap or GaussianLSI/T2 conclusion is added.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert E with canonical volume and Borel structure, including dimension zero.</li><li>Unchanged source normalization kappa&gt;=1, global C2 V with Hessian kappa^-1 I..I; measurable eta/y family S and every eta(s)&gt;0 with no cap.</li><li>S/measurable-family scope is an authored extension. Constant Unit families recover printed fixed parameters. No stationary point, actual probability law, partition, density or domain certificates are public inputs.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Reuse the true posterior and the same stationary point</h4><p>The existing allpositive true standardized RGO producer constructs a measurable p with p+eta gradVp=y. Its literal affine pushforward r is the actual volume Gibbs law of norm²/2+rho, and its residual is C2 with gradientrho0=0 and Hessian0..eta. The residual value at0 is computed from its definition.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[p_s+\eta_s\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\quad r_s=(x\mapsto\eta_s^{-1/2}(x-p_s))_\#R_s,\quad\rho_s(u)=V(p_s+\sqrt{\eta_s}u)-V(p_s)-\sqrt{\eta_s}\langle\nabla V(p_s),u\rangle.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Apply the new density-domain producer to that actual residual</h4><p>Instantiate the shared theorem with L=eta(s) and the same actual rho. Its canonical volume-law equality agrees with the true affine posterior law, yielding r=gamma.tilted(-rho), the actual normalized q, all square-root/entropy domains and actual probability. No output density or moment certificate is supplied.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[0&lt;Z_s\le1,\quad q_s=e^{-\rho_s}/Z_s,\quad f_s=e^{-\rho_s/2}/\sqrt{Z_s},\quad r_s=q_s\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>GaussianSqrtDensityDomain.gaussian_sqrt_density_domain; actual htrue</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Keep the same law in every derivative and energy conclusion</h4><p>Transport only measure-valued fields along the proved actual-law equality. f_s and both gradients retain their literal representatives, and the exact1/4 energy uses that same true r_s. The measurable family is an authored extension; fixed parameters follow by Unit specialization. No eta upper cap or GaussianLSI/T2 conclusion is added.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\nabla f_s=-\tfrac12f_s\nabla\rho_s,\quad\nabla\log q_s=-\nabla\rho_s,\quad\int\|\nabla f_s\|^2d\gamma=\frac14\int\|\nabla\rho_s\|^2dr_s\qquad(\eta_s&gt;0).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>actual hprob/hρlp/henergy transported along htrue; literal source family definitions</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain"><summary>Lean statement · standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain</summary><p>For the true source RGO posterior standardized using the same internally produced measurable stationary proximal point, produce the actual relative Gaussian density, positive partition, C2 square root and all L2/entropy/gradient domains with the exact1/4 energy, for every eta(s)&gt;0.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      let gamma := stdGaussian E
      let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
      let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
      let f := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u/2)/Real.sqrt (Z s)
      ∀ s, 0 &lt; Z s ∧ Z s ≤ 1 ∧
        r s = gamma.tilted (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) ∧
        r s = gamma.withDensity (fun u =&gt; ENNReal.ofReal (q s u)) ∧
        IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧
        (∀ u, 0 &lt; q s u ∧ f s u^2 = q s u) ∧
        (∫ u, q s u ∂gamma) = 1 ∧
        ContDiff ℝ 2 (f s) ∧ MemLp (f s) 2 gamma ∧
        MemLp (gradient (f s)) 2 gamma ∧ MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧
        Integrable (fun u =&gt; q s u*Real.log (q s u)) gamma ∧
        (∀ u, gradient (f s) u = -(f s u/2) • gradient (rho s) u) ∧
        (∀ u, gradient (fun z =&gt; Real.log (q s z)) u = -gradient (rho s) u) ∧
        (∫ u, ‖gradient (f s) u‖^2 ∂gamma) =
          (1/4 : ℝ)*(∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s)</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgosqrtdensity.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain"><summary>Lean proof · standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain</summary><p>Reuse the true posterior and the same stationary point; Apply the new density-domain producer to that actual residual; Keep the same law in every derivative and energy conclusion</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      let gamma := stdGaussian E
      let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
      let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
      let f := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u/2)/Real.sqrt (Z s)
      ∀ s, 0 &lt; Z s ∧ Z s ≤ 1 ∧
        r s = gamma.tilted (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) ∧
        r s = gamma.withDensity (fun u =&gt; ENNReal.ofReal (q s u)) ∧
        IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧
        (∀ u, 0 &lt; q s u ∧ f s u^2 = q s u) ∧
        (∫ u, q s u ∂gamma) = 1 ∧
        ContDiff ℝ 2 (f s) ∧ MemLp (f s) 2 gamma ∧
        MemLp (gradient (f s)) 2 gamma ∧ MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧
        Integrable (fun u =&gt; q s u*Real.log (q s u)) gamma ∧
        (∀ u, gradient (f s) u = -(f s u/2) • gradient (rho s) u) ∧
        (∀ u, gradient (fun z =&gt; Real.log (q s z)) u = -gradient (rho s) u) ∧
        (∫ u, ‖gradient (f s) u‖^2 ∂gamma) =
          (1/4 : ℝ)*(∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) := by
  obtain ⟨p,hpm,heq,hparent⟩ :=
    StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher hκ hV hH heta hy hpos
  let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
    Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
  let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
  let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
  let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
  let gamma := stdGaussian E
  let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
  let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
  let f := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u/2)/Real.sqrt (Z s)
  refine ⟨p,hpm,heq,?_⟩
  change ∀ s, 0 &lt; Z s ∧ Z s ≤ 1 ∧ _
  intro s
  obtain ⟨_hRp,hρ,_hQ,hρgrad,_hQgrad,hρH,_hQH,hlaw,_hrest⟩ := hparent.2 s
  have hρzero : rho s 0 = 0 := by simp [rho]
  let L : ℝ≥0 := ⟨eta s,(hpos s).le⟩
  have hHρ : ∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ (L : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 := hρH
  have hg := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSqrtDensityDomain.gaussian_sqrt_density_domain
    hρ hρzero hρgrad hHρ
  obtain ⟨hZ,hZone,hvolume,hdensity,hprob,hfq,hqone,hf,hflp,hfglp,hρlp,he,hdf,hdlog,henergy⟩ := hg
  have htrue : r s=gamma.tilted (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) := hlaw.trans hvolume.symm
  have hprob&#x27; : IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) := htrue.symm ▸ hprob
  have hρlp&#x27; : MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) := htrue.symm ▸ hρlp
  have henergy&#x27; : (∫ u, ‖gradient (f s) u‖^2 ∂gamma) =
      (1/4 : ℝ)*(∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) := htrue.symm ▸ henergy
  exact ⟨hZ,hZone,htrue,htrue.trans hdensity,hprob&#x27;,hfq,hqone,hf,hflp,hfglp,hρlp&#x27;,
    he,hdf,hdlog,henergy&#x27;⟩

end
end AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgosqrtdensity.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Actual positive Gaussian relative-density and classical C2/L2 square-root/entropy/log-gradient/Dirichlet=Fisher/4 domains, genuinely consumed by the source standardized true RGO. No Gaussian LSI/T2/KL weak representative/Sobolev adapter/W2/bias/fullLemma/main/work/composition credit. Focused3748 passed with E0/L0 and actual eta2y3 posterior tests, standard3 axioms only. Independent proof/blind/source/commit review and integration pending; postmerge purification, renderedQA and Copy/Download remain open.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositionfisher.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositio-ff78a6f59e"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-gaussiansqrtdensitydomain-gaussian-sqrt-density-domain.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSqrtDensityDomain.gaussian_sqrt_density_domain</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><p class="muted">No direct Mathlib call recorded; see the Samplinglib parents.</p><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8">Actual source residual and omitted analytic prerequisites</a> — Actual positive Gaussian relative-density and classical C2/L2 square-root/entropy/log-gradient/Dirichlet=Fisher/4 domains, genuinely consumed by the source standardized true RGO. No Gaussian LSI/T2/KL weak representative/Sobolev adapter/W2/bias/fullLemma/main/work/composition credit. Focused3748 passed with E0/L0 and actual eta2y3 posterior tests, standard3 axioms only. Independent proof/blind/source/commit review and integration pending; postmerge purification, renderedQA and Copy/Download remain open.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
